the movie is set in 1862 and it revolves  around Elizabeth lib right she is an  English nurse who is sent to a tiny  Irish village to observe an 11 year old  girl named Anna O'Donnell Anna's family  has made an unbelievable claim that she  has not consumed any food since the last  four months yet she is perfectly healthy  and fine given the cost of my recent  grocery bills I too would love to know  how Anna does it in the first scene lib  arrives in Ireland and makes her way  into a lodge where she will stay for the  entirety of her visit the next day she  is taken to a place where the village  committee is waiting for her lib learns  that she will be assisted in her  Endeavor by a religious nun named sister  Michael the committee consists of a  medical practitioner a priest and some  other important people of the town the  meeting starts and lib and sister  Michael are instructed to keep watch on  the girl Anna with the help of routine  8-hour shifts for two weeks on the 14th  day they are to report their findings to  the committee members which will finally  reveal if Anna has supernatural  abilities before ending the meeting the  committee also warns lib and sister  Michael to not confer with each other  about the case afterwards lib travels to  the O'Donnell residence with the medical  practitioner Dr mcbriarty which lies on  the outskirts of the village there lib  meets the extremely religious family of  Anna which consists of her parents and  older sister Kitty it turns out the  little girl receives visitors from all  parts of the country who are Keen to  witness her Miracle after the visitors  leave I mean leave lib oh gosh after the  visitors leave lib goes upstairs and  finds Anna in a healthy state but  strangely the little girl keeps on  praying after every hour as if she is  asking for something when asked a better  secret Anna claims that she consumes  Mana from Heaven to remain alive  according to the Bible Mana is an edible  substance which God apparently used to  distribute later at dinner lib notices a  family photograph which also includes a  young man on inquiring she learns that  he was lib's elder brother who passed  away a few years ago due to a mysterious  illness the same night before going to  bed lib is seen taking some kind of  liquid hallucinogen which she keeps in a  small pocket along with some baby boots  after taking the supposed drug she  pricks her finger draws blood from it  and then licks it she does this every  night before sleeping in order to cope  with her stress and past traumas which  are not specified but probably have to  do with being some sort of vampire  hippie the next day lib takes Anna out  into the fields for a walk before  examining her room to check if there are  any places which can be used to hide  food however she doesn't find anything  suspicious while leaving lib expresses  her concern to Dr mcbrearty about the  large number of visitors that Anna gets  she asserts that for a serious study  Anna needs some quiet and isolation to  which the doctor agrees the following  morning while having breakfast lib meets  a guy named William Byrne a local man  who now works as a journalist for the  Daily Telegram in London William  mentions that he's been sent by the  company to interview the miracle girl  Anna however Liv informs him that Anna  is not taking visitors from now on as  per the doctor's request later at the  O'Donnell household lib chats within his  sister Kitty and learns that the last  thing Anna had eaten was wheat and bread  it turns out that it was on her 11th  birthday that night as lib is keeping  watch over the little girl she fiddles  around with one of her toys and  accidentally breaks it surprisingly she  finds a lock of hair inside which is  revealed to be of Anna's late brother  the next morning lib apologizes for  breaking the toy and proceeds to strike  up a friendly conversation with the  hopes of establishing a friendship with  the young girl she does so by giving her  a pet name man before introducing her  own name in the afternoon lib helps  Santa dress up and takes her out for a  walk the latter slowly becomes  accustomed to her new friend and starts  opening up from their conversation we  get to know lib had served in the  Crimean War she saw many soldiers suffer  and die and this is why she experiences  bouts of depression at times however  despite this lib says that she feels  very privileged to be with people even  when they die on the way back home Anna  stumbles upon William who is still in  town due to his boss's daily demand for  information regarding the miracle child  here's a headline Willy boy shove it up  your ass he presses lib for information  and the latter finally reveals that  nothing but water has passed through  Anna's lips in the past few days however  William doesn't believe it and calls the  whole thing a hoax as the days pass lib  notices something strange every night  before bed Anna's family prays with her  and the mother even kisses her mouth as  part of the ritual suspecting that it  has something to do with the whole case  one day lib banishes the family from  getting in contact with Anna she lies  that it is a requirement of the watch as  per Dr mcbriarty's orders the family  becomes very distressed because of the  new rule surprisingly the very next day  Anna's Health begins to decline possibly  because of the lack of nutrition in her  body lib informs the journalist William  about it and the two decide to wait  until something conclusive comes up the  same day as lib carries out her regular  inspection and checkup of Anna she finds  out that the little girl's teeth are  decaying and that one has already fallen  out on her way back home Liv meets  Anna's sister Kitty and the two strike  up a conversation Kitty reveals that she  and William were once close friends  before he was sent to school in England  he studied for years and returned but by  that time his entire family had perished  due to the Great Famine hearing this a  shocked lib returns to the lodge and  tries to comfort William one thing leads  to another and the two end up having  coitus I wonder if they also drank each  other's blood the next morning as the  two talk about their past Liv reveals  that she had previously given birth  however just after two weeks the baby  died and her husband disappeared soon  after this is the main reason she  decided to leave for the Crimea War  later in the afternoon lib takes Anna  out for a walk and introduces him to  William the little girl is skeptical  about the meeting but William eventually  wins her trust by giving her a  thamatrope toy unfortunately that  evening Anna's well-being gets even  worse so lib requests her parents give  her something to eat however they refuse  to do so claiming that Anna had  previously sworn to never eat again left  with no choice lib heads over to Dr  mcbriarty's office and explains the  situation to him she requests that he  convinced the committee to stop the  watch but Dr mcbriarty refuses he claims  that Anna is converting sunlight into  energy and so they have nothing to worry  about before the meeting ends he orders  lib to do her job which is only to keep  watch and not to diagnose Anna anymore  one day during her shift lib is unable  to see Anna suffer and becomes desperate  to save her as a result she goes  downstairs and asks for a bowl of soup  for herself lib then proceeds to force  feed Anna by shoving a tube down her  throat however when the little girl  continues to cry and Revolt she realizes  her mistake and withdraws the tube at  this point Anna has started having  difficulties in breathing celeb Comforts  her and profusely apologizes a few hours  later William and lib take Anna out for  a walk hoping that the fresh air can  cure her ailment as they wander around  the beautiful landscape William informs  lib that he has already submitted his  report titled Murder By degrees in which  he 