eve her even  her partner sister Michael denies seeing  anything suspicious later Anna and her  parents are also called for a proper  questioning but as expected the cunning  parents deny feeding Anna anything other  than Mana from Heaven this results in  the continuation of the watch and Anna's  health keeps on deteriorating one day  she vomits and struggles to stay upright  a devastated lib tries to convince  Anna's mother to feed the little girl  and take her to a doctor but to no avail  why doesn't Anna just sneak in some  goddamn Oreos or something left with no  choice lib devises a plan to free Anna  and help her Escape From The Wretched  house she plots the whole thing with her  new lover William as he too is worried  for Anna the scene then cuts to the next  day where lib is preparing to take Anna  from her home after a while the entire  family goes outside to attend a mass and  taking this is the perfect opportunity  lib puts her plan into motion since she  knows that the little girl will not  agree to eat food or seek treatment from  a doctor lib starts talking to her in a  religious manner she tells her to  believe that Anna will die and a new  girl named Nan will take her place and  live on to be her Anna who is on the  verge of death smiles and agrees with  this approval lib carries her on her  back to a nearby well and tells her that  Anna is now free to go to heaven and  meet God the little girl smiles one last  time and closes her eyes shortly after  she wakes up reborn as Nan she seems to  have changed her personality as well and  is more helpful and happy than before  where's that poutine at she says  moreover when lib gives her some food  she eats it without any hesitation this  indicates that the little girl is now  ready to move on from her old religious  life after Anna is out of danger lib  leaves her there and heads to the  O'Donnell residence she then confidently  begins pouring kerosene all over Anna's  room before setting it on fire however  in the process she accidentally injures  her hands in no time the entire house is  set alight and lib Falls unconscious as  soon as she gets out following the  incident we see lib in front of the  committee members with severely burnt  arms and a rough face she hands them her  report diary which she is modified to  fake Anna's death when one of the  members asks what's happened lib replies  that she went inside the little girl's  room and saw her dead and in a State of  Shock she knocked over a burn lamp which  ultimately set the O'Donnell household  on fire unfortunately none of the  committee members are convinced with her  story and decide that she will remain in  the village until further notice they  also decide to not pair as she was  unsuccessful in solving the mystery  after all a few days passed by and the  lib is finally released from her  obligations and is free to travel back  to London before leaving sister Michael  undresses her wounds and treats her one  last time she tells lib that she had  left the mass early that day and she saw  what she believed was a vision of Anna  with an angel riding a horse in reality  she saw the little girl being taken away  by the journalist William sister Michael  then asks lib to promise her that Anna  has gone to a better place lib promises  and the scene cuts to her returning back  to London where's that horse William at  there she follows a piece of paper with  an address presumably given to her by  William shortly after she reaches the  place but doesn't find anyone nearby  suddenly she hears a knock from a window  into her surprise she sees Anna all  healthy and well she also reunites with  William and the three take a family  photo in the final scene they board a  ship to Sydney and all three of them  changed their names to make sure that  their past lives don't come back to  haunt them the movie ends with lib and  William happily looking at Anna stuffing  her little cheeks  subscribe for more videos like this 